    "evidence_text": "A considerable subgroup of patients with early breast cancer does not address benefits of anthracycline based chemotherapy.\n\nIn multivariate Cox regression analysis MVD was independently associated with DFS.\n\nHyaluronan impairs vascular function and drug delivery in a mouse model of pancreatic cancer\n\nCXCR7 knockdown resulted in the inhibition of IL6-induced proliferation and chemoresistance.\n\nTumor-associated macrophages (TAM) contribute to all aspects of tumor progression.\n\nHere, we have identified the mechanism that limited the effect of CSF1R targeted therapy.\n\nWe surmise that such 'viral mimicry' constitutes a hallmark of successful chemotherapy.\n\nA CXCL1 Paracrine Network Links Cancer Chemoresistance and Metastasis\n\nCXCR2 blockers break this cycle, augmenting the efficacy of chemotherapy against breast tumors and particularly against metastasis.\n\nInhibition of Hedgehog signaling enhances delivery of chemotherapy in a mouse model of pancreatic cancer.\n\nThus, inefficient drug delivery may be an important contributor to chemoresistance in pancreatic cancer.\n\nPreclinical investigations suggest increased activity of cilengitide in combination with other treatment modalities.\n\nHypoxia was found to be a heterogeneous property of human tumors.\n\nHowever, hypoxia often occurred without necrosis.",
